Intro to Python: Module 1 Basics

1. Output and Syntax
print("Sophia Codes") # String output
print(360)            # Numerical output

2. Memory and Variables
item = "Bike"         # String variable
country = "France"    # Note: Strings must be in quotes
print(item)

3. Numerical Data and Operations
print(6 + 2)          # Addition
print(10 - 5)         # Subtraction
print(2 * 3)          # Multiplication

 4. Working with Variable Data
budget = 200
print(budget)

budget = 20           # Reassigning variable
print(budget + 10)    # Math with variables (Result: 30)

price = 5
amount = 3
print(price * amount) # Multiplication with variables (Result: 15)

 5. Updating Values (The "Latest Value" Rule)
price = 98
price = 100           # Overwriting the previous value
print(price)          # This will show 100
